select set_config('unimate.system','on',true);
values ('aabu', 'جامعة آل البيت', 'Al al-Bayt University', 'المفرق', 'public', array['aabu.edu.jo']::text[], 32.361, 36.219, 'draft', 'Majors assembled from individual college pages plus the 2025/2026 direct-admission and parallel-program announcements and the finance-department fee table (the consolidated list web2.aabu.edu.jo/regDepartment/bs.jsp could not be fetched). Name variants on the site: the business college is called ''كلية الاقتصاد والعلوم الادارية'' on the colleges index but ''كلية إدارة المال والأعمال'' in the fee table; law degree appears as ''القانون'' (fee table) and ''الحقوق'' (2025/26 announcement); architecture appears as ''هندسة العمارة'' in admission tables and ''هندسة العمارة والفنون الإسلامية'' on the engineering page. Arts college is ''كلية الاداب'' on the index, ''كلية الآداب والعلوم الإنسانية'' in the fee table. Not included: ''الإمامة والوعظ والإرشاد'' (Sharia; only seen in older 2017/18 pages and fee table, current status unverified), ''نظم المعلومات المحاسبية'' and ''نظم المعلومات المالية والمصرفية'' (only in fee table, current status unverified). IT college has a ''تكنولوجيا المعلومات'' department but no matching bachelor programme was listed. Medical analysis (التحاليل الطبية) is listed under the Science college in the fee table but now has a department page under Applied Medical Sciences. Institute of Astronomy and Higher Institute of Islamic Studies appear to be graduate-only and are omitted. A ''كلية التعليم التقني'' offering diplomas exists (2025 announcement) but its diploma list is only in a PDF brochure that was not readable, so no diplomas are included. Email: staff domain aabu.edu.jo confirmed (info@aabu.edu.jo, Outlook OWA link); student email domain/subdomain not verified. Coordinates from Wikipedia (32°21′40″N 36°13′08″E), not OSM. Colours per Wikipedia are green and white; no hex verified. English names are translations, not official.')
